    {
      "question": "e-21692",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "795075c949198773b7c734d608896c975fdf201882cf2a83934b2561442cdbc2",
      "new_sha256": "0946ce38c5bb26ff9024e4f8eed7b1331bd6fa32db0efdb8839bf464be9bd86a",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21692",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}(t)=3x(t)-2y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}(t)=4x(t)+y(t)-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[1, \\, 2]^T.$ What is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?",
