    {
      "question": "e-21693",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "15cfdb2192b845c88e4485ab51381c796b3160e24c3a19557bd201557c9f631a",
      "new_sha256": "1b5fe0747050e4120b4cbabfbcdeb2f0d156feb3ce9080c7723007c73b6c306f",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21693",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To shift the system's equilibrium from $\\mathbf{x}^\\ast$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} \n= \\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{x}^\\ast,\n$$\n\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069931/assets/951509e719a40caba7ecc5872d983b6cf83128d77af670c88846d2a06d329d8e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069931/assets/a3d02714f52ce42ec3e6d78d9cdd91f4c2ca14a59948f078d93318c94ec5e31a.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069931/assets/cce8b4b07839490b3be0841f8a4e6e73b69426426504625cedecf738947b046d.png)\n\nIn coordinate form, this can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx(t) = u(t), \\qquad\ny(t) = v(t) - 2, \\qquad\nx'(t) = u'(t), \\qquad\nv'(t) = y'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now substitute these into the given system.\n\n- Substituting into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032}(t) & ={x}^{2}(t)+x(t)+y(t)+2 \\\\ {u}^{\u2032}(t) & ={u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+(v(t)-2)+2 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substituting into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}(t) & =5x(t)-{y}^{2}(t)+3y(t)+10 \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}(t) & =5u(t)-(v(t)-2)^{2}+3(v(t)-2)+10 \\\\  & =5u(t)-({v}^{2}(t)-4v(t)+4)+3v(t)-6+10 \\\\  & =5u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+7v(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{\u2032}(t)={u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}(t)=5u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+7v(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069931/example-21693.json",
          "file_sha256": "8239f83f05eb4940ac6143e9c7fdf0fde55ad946880498ad5996fb075cbfc106"
        }
      ],
